<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bonabeau-social-wasp-comb-hexagons-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Karsai & Pénzes (1993) J. Theor. Biol., Theraulaz & Bonabeau (1995) Science & Smith et al. (2021) PNAS stigmergic hexagonal wasp comb architecture, shared-wall pulp economy & 5-7 topological disclination pairs — MorphoEval overall 53.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `1998-bonabeau-social-wasp-comb-hexagons.py` (overall weighted score: 56.2/100). The v1 script implements the analytic centered hexagonal ring progression N(R) = 1 + 3R(R+1), total wall count W(R) = 3N(R) + 6R + 3, and wall-to-cell ratio W(R)/N(R) -> 3.0 across R in [0, 7], but generates cells via deterministic ringenumeration rather than simulating the stochastic Boltzmann stigmergic initiation rule P_init(k) ~ exp(beta*k) over k in {1, 2, 3} shared-wall perimeter pockets, omits the 7-point beta selectivity sweep and beta = 0 Eden random growth negative control, omits the Smith et al. (2021) worker-to-queen cell size transition inducing paired 5-7 topological defects, and never loads or segments the vendored Polistes wasp comb specimen (`polistes_wasp_comb_specimen.jpg`). Overall 53.5/100 (faithfulness 47.1, reproducibility 68.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit e93f00e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 57, Morphological realism / specimen match 35, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 52, Source and data traceability 74, Code-to-model traceability 68, Reproducibility package 64. Output judged: docs/media/social_wasp_comb_hexagons_comparison.png: rendered output of 1998-bonabeau-social-wasp-comb-hexagons.py at e93f00e, image/png, 258873 B, 1890×1400 px, artifact_sha256 75731e309cf80570ed6a43e2e3b7fc9cab06affe9904e112072395a8db5fcd5d (sha256 75731e309cf80570ed6a43e2e3b7fc9cab06affe9904e112072395a8db5fcd5d), spec_fingerprint 6471896f9ec341c70d5d90fdfc768c186b2e5e7ed95f0e8568fe6372d790ffc3. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6471896f9ec341c70d5d90fdfc768c186b2e5e7ed95f0e8568fe6372d790ffc3; artifact_sha256: 75731e309cf80570ed6a43e2e3b7fc9cab06affe9904e112072395a8db5fcd5d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/social_wasp_comb_hexagons/paper_citations.bib=9b09023aaea52aa7..., datasets/social_wasp_comb_hexagons/polistes_wasp_comb_specimen.jpg=03befd4d1fbfa35a..., datasets/social_wasp_comb_hexagons/scout_manifest.json=63f51b932c469536..., datasets/social_wasp_comb_hexagons/social_wasp_comb_hexagons_reference.json=5d67bfb268fa3003...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement both the 8-ring concentric comb economy trajectory R in [0, 7] (verifying W(R)/N(R) -> 3.0 and 50% pulp savings) and the 7-point stigmergic selectivity sweep beta in [0.0, 5.5] including the beta = 0.0 Eden random branched comb negative control.",
        "remediation needed: Implement the Smith et al. (2021) PNAS worker-to-reproductive cell size transition (lambda in [1.00, 1.40]) with spring-Voronoi lattice relaxation inducing paired pentagon-heptagon (5-7) topological disclinations with zero net Euler charge.",
        "remediation needed: Replace deterministic ring enumeration with a stochastic Karsai-Penzes & Theraulaz-Bonabeau 2D/3D hexagonal lattice builder implementing Boltzmann stigmergic pocket selection P_init(j) = exp(beta * k_j) / sum_m exp(beta * k_m) over k in {1, 2, 3} shared-wall perimeter pockets.",
        "remediation needed: Segment the vendored CC BY 2.0 Polistes paper wasp comb photograph (`polistes_wasp_comb_specimen.jpg`) via Difference-of-Gaussians cavity detection and Delaunay/Voronoi topology to extract brood cell count and interior coordination number <z>, and enforce runtime SHA-256 verification." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.35e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

